WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.115
An art corner.

2
00:00:01.275 --> 00:00:04.200
An art corner is a small gallery in your classroom.

3
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.193
It holds art from far away and from long ago.

4
00:00:07.353 --> 00:00:09.396
It holds your work and your friends' work.

5
00:00:09.556 --> 00:00:11.646
It is a place to look and get ideas.

6
00:00:12.346 --> 00:00:13.182
Group it.

7
00:00:13.342 --> 00:00:15.525
You can group the art in lots of ways.

8
00:00:15.685 --> 00:00:16.614
By colour.

9
00:00:16.774 --> 00:00:17.842
By feeling.

10
00:00:18.002 --> 00:00:21.485
By how it was made: printed, woven, clay or collage.

11
00:00:21.645 --> 00:00:24.245
Grouping helps people see how the works connect.

12
00:00:24.945 --> 00:00:25.921
Connect it.

13
00:00:26.081 --> 00:00:29.006
A cloth from Ghana and a tiled wall look different.

14
00:00:29.166 --> 00:00:33.578
But both have a pattern that repeats, and both put their shapes in squares.

15
00:00:33.738 --> 00:00:36.850
Finding the idea two works share is called connecting.

16
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.525
Look back.

17
00:00:38.685 --> 00:00:41.193
Your journal holds everything you made this year.

18
00:00:41.353 --> 00:00:42.653
Look back through it.

19
00:00:42.813 --> 00:00:44.067
Your first print.

20
00:00:44.227 --> 00:00:45.434
Your first weave.

21
00:00:45.594 --> 00:00:46.709
Your clay dog.

22
00:00:46.869 --> 00:00:48.355
See how far you have come.
